---
import DocumentationLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro';
import PreviewControls from './PreviewControls.astro';
import MerchantCardPreview from './MerchantCardPreview.astro';
import {CodeSnippet} from '../dmf-ui/code-block';
import {blocks} from '../../data/blocks';
import catalog from '../../../contracts/catalog.json';
const block=blocks.find(b=>b.slug==='merchant-card')!,record=catalog.blocks.find(b=>b.slug==='merchant-card')!,react=catalog.react.blocks.find(b=>b.name==='MerchantCard')!;
---
<DocumentationLayout title="MerchantCard" description={block.description} section="blocks" crumbs={[{name:'Blocks',href:'/blocks/'},{name:'MerchantCard'}]} toc={[{id:'preview',title:'Reference preview'},{id:'usage',title:'Usage'},{id:'api',title:'API and ownership'},{id:'design',title:'Design mapping'},{id:'acceptance',title:'Acceptance'}]}>
 <h1>MerchantCard</h1><p class="docs-lead">{block.description}</p>
 <section id="preview" class="docs-section"><h2>Reference preview</h2><PreviewControls/><MerchantCardPreview/></section>
 <section id="usage" class="docs-section"><h2>Usage</h2><p>Import the adapter stylesheet once and render in .dmf-ui. Copy the supplied SVG icon files from dmf-ui/assets/merchant-card into your host's public asset directory, or import each URL through your bundler in Astro. Supply those four URLs as icons. Host-owned URLs keep native SSR and client hydration consistent across frameworks; no temporary Figma URL is used at runtime.</p><CodeSnippet code={`---\nimport {MerchantCard} from 'dmf-ui/blocks';\nimport verified from 'dmf-ui/assets/merchant-card/verified.svg?url';\nimport hours from 'dmf-ui/assets/merchant-card/hours.svg?url';\nimport distance from 'dmf-ui/assets/merchant-card/distance.svg?url';\nimport star from 'dmf-ui/assets/merchant-card/star.svg?url';\nconst icons={verified,hours,distance,star};\n---\n<MerchantCard id="merchant" name="Sample merchant" href="#merchant-details"\n  photos={[]} icons={icons}/>\n<!-- The host must render the merchant-details destination. -->`} language="astro" title="Astro MerchantCard" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={`import {MerchantCard,MerchantListingBlock} from '@dmf-ui/react';\nimport '@dmf-ui/react/styles.css';\n\nconst icons={verified:'/merchant-card/verified.svg',hours:'/merchant-card/hours.svg',\n  distance:'/merchant-card/distance.svg',star:'/merchant-card/star.svg'};\n\n<MerchantListingBlock id="results" title="Merchants" items={merchants}\n  getItemKey={merchant=>merchant.id}\n  renderItem={merchant=><MerchantCard {...merchant} icons={icons}/>}/>;`} language="tsx" title="React listing integration" wrap/></section>
 <section id="api" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>API and ownership</h2><p>id, name, href, photos and the four local icon URLs are required. headingLevel defaults to h3 (h2/h3/h4). Up to three authored photos use source order and object-cover crops. Empty photos render photoFallback. Hosts supply alternatives and image load/error policy; no image loader or network service is added.</p><p>Optional verified/status/distance/price/cuisine/address/rating/review data is not fabricated. verified is a host assertion with configurable verifiedLabel; statusTone styles text without calculating business hours. Price level is 1–5, with an accessible priceLabel and decorative dollar symbols. Rating is 0–5 and reviewCount a nonnegative integer; the display rounds the score to one decimal at most and formats reviews using locale. Labels are configurable.</p><p>One native link, named by the merchant heading, covers the card through a noninteractive overlay. Rating, price and verification are read-only summaries, not extra buttons. Do not nest controls inside this composition. Native article props/ref remain available; no arbitrary children are accepted. Use MerchantListingBlock's item renderer for a different card anatomy.</p><CodeSnippet code={record.declaration} language="ts" title="Astro Props" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={react.types[0].declaration} language="ts" title="React Props" wrap/></section>
 <section id="design" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Design mapping</h2><p>The owner-selected HUI node 1:597 defines a 328px reference width, three square photos, 1px dividers, 16px outer corners, 12px footer inset, 16px Inter merchant heading, 12px details and a 58×40px review badge. The original four SVGs retain their intrinsic dimensions and colors. Reference photos remain supplied data rather than component defaults. Card and Text are reused; the existing multi-star Rating does not express the source's one-star/two-row badge without changing its API, so this compact read-only summary is local composition.</p><p>Nova/Neutral remains the default. HUI-specific grayscale mappings and Inter name styling are scoped to this card. The reference hours text is #1B998B at about 3.51:1 on white; the text uses the documented derived #14796E mapping (about 5.26:1) while the original clock asset stays unchanged. This is an accessibility adaptation, not a newly claimed official brand value. White CB/HUI primary-action exceptions remain unchanged.</p><p>The card fills its host width, scales the photo strip, wraps long merchant names and metadata, and retains the full address in the DOM while visually ellipsizing that line. The native destination exposes complete details. Standard RTL mirrors logical layout without enlarging text. Focus outlines remain visible in forced colors.</p></section>
 <section id="acceptance" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Acceptance and limitations</h2><p>{block.limitations}</p><p>Reference text and numbers are authored design content, not verified current business facts. Packed Astro/React consumers and MerchantListingBlock integration verify reuse independently of documentation. Browser evidence is scoped; no Safari/Firefox, spoken-reader, physical-device or live-business acceptance is implied. <a href="/docs/architecture/">Architecture and ownership</a>.</p><p>Sources: <code>{record.source}</code>, <code>{react.source}</code>. <a href="https://www.figma.com/design/M9PisJq2AJbRpgMbzxyvmO?node-id=1-597">Selected design node</a>.</p></section>
</DocumentationLayout>
